== 2.8 Chapter 2 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The site of aerobic respiration in a cell is the],
  [Golgi apparatus],
  [ribosome],
  [mitochondrion],
  [nucleus]
)

#mcq(2, [Which structure is present in a plant cell but not in an animal cell?],
  [Nucleus],
  [Chloroplast],
  [Mitochondrion],
  [Ribosome]
)

#mcq(3, [The organelle that packages and secretes proteins is the],
  [smooth endoplasmic reticulum],
  [Golgi apparatus],
  [ribosome],
  [lysosome]
)

#mcq(4, [A prokaryotic cell lacks],
  [DNA],
  [ribosomes],
  [a cell membrane],
  [membrane-bound organelles]
)

#mcq(5, [The cell membrane is described as partially permeable because],
  [it has no pores],
  [it lets only some substances through],
  [it is made of cellulose],
  [it lets everything through]
)

#mcq(6, [The cell wall of a plant is fully permeable and is made of],
  [lipid],
  [protein],
  [chitin],
  [cellulose]
)

#mcq(7, [Which organelle contains digestive enzymes and digests worn-out organelles?],
  [Lysosome],
  [Vacuole],
  [Ribosome],
  [Centriole]
)

#mcq(8, [The function of the nucleus is to],
  [package secretions],
  [release energy],
  [make proteins],
  [contain the chromosomes and control the cell]
)

#mcq(9, [The cell theory states that],
  [cells arise spontaneously],
  [all cells have a nucleus],
  [cells are all the same size],
  [all living things are made of cells and new cells come from existing cells]
)

#mcq(10, [A plant cell placed in pure water does not burst because],
  [the cell wall resists the pressure as the cell becomes turgid],
  [it has no membrane],
  [water cannot enter],
  [the vacuole is empty]
)

#mcq(11, [Centrioles are found in animal cells and are involved in],
  [protein synthesis],
  [digestion],
  [photosynthesis],
  [forming spindle fibres during cell division]
)

#mcq(12, [Which structure controls what enters and leaves a cell?],
  [Cytoplasm],
  [Cell membrane],
  [Cell wall],
  [Nucleus]
)

#mcq(13, [Chlorophyll is contained in the],
  [nucleolus],
  [chloroplasts],
  [ribosomes],
  [mitochondria]
)

#mcq(14, [The jelly-like material in which the organelles are suspended is the],
  [matrix],
  [cytoplasm],
  [nucleoplasm],
  [stroma]
)

#mcq(15, [Which of these is the correct order of the levels of organisation from simplest to most complex?],
  [Tissue → cell → organ → organism],
  [Cell → tissue → organ → system],
  [System → organ → cell → tissue],
  [Organ → tissue → cell → system]
)

#mcq(16, [A group of similar cells performing the same function is a],
  [tissue],
  [organelle],
  [system],
  [organ]
)

#mcq(17, [The main difference between a bacterium and a plant cell is that a bacterium],
  [has no true nucleus and no membrane-bound organelles],
  [has no cell membrane],
  [has no DNA],
  [cannot reproduce]
)

