=== Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "C", dense: true)[
  The mitochondrion releases energy from glucose by aerobic respiration; its inner membrane is folded into cristae to increase surface area.
]

#sol-item(2, "B", dense: true)[
  Chloroplasts, the cellulose cell wall and a large central vacuole are the plant features.
]

#sol-item(3, "B", dense: true)[
  The Golgi body modifies, packages and secretes substances made in the cell.
]

#sol-item(4, "D", dense: true)[
  Prokaryotes have no nucleus and no membrane-bound organelles, though they do have ribosomes, a membrane and DNA.
]

#sol-item(5, "B", dense: true)[
  Selective permeability is what allows the cell to control what enters and leaves.
]

#sol-item(6, "D", dense: true)[
  Cellulose gives the wall its strength; chitin is the fungal equivalent.
]

#sol-item(7, "A", dense: true)[
  The lysosome is the cell's digestive compartment, common in animal cells.
]

#sol-item(8, "D", dense: true)[
  The nucleus holds the DNA and so directs all the activities of the cell.
]

#sol-item(9, "D", dense: true)[
  Three statements: all organisms are made of cells; the cell is the basic unit of life; new cells arise only from existing cells.
]

#sol-item(10, "A", dense: true)[
  The rigid cellulose wall limits expansion, so the cell becomes turgid instead of bursting.
]

#sol-item(11, "D", dense: true)[
  Centrioles organise the spindle during cell division; higher plant cells generally lack them.
]

#sol-item(12, "B", dense: true)[
  The partially permeable membrane, not the fully permeable wall, does the controlling.
]

#sol-item(13, "B", dense: true)[
  Chloroplasts contain the chlorophyll that traps light for photosynthesis.
]

#sol-item(14, "B", dense: true)[
  Cytoplasm — the site of many of the cell's chemical reactions.
]

#sol-item(15, "B", dense: true)[
  Cell → tissue → organ → system → organism.
]

#sol-item(16, "A", dense: true)[
  A tissue is a group of similar cells with a shared function, such as muscle tissue.
]

#sol-item(17, "A", dense: true)[
  That is the prokaryote/eukaryote distinction; bacteria do have DNA, a membrane and a cell wall, but of peptidoglycan.
]

#sol-item(18, "C", dense: true)[
  There is no light in the soil, so chloroplasts would be useless; the cell is adapted for absorption instead.
]

#sol-item(19, "D", dense: true)[
  The nucleolus is the site of ribosome manufacture.
]

#sol-item(20, "C", dense: true)[
  Active transport needs energy, supplied by the mitochondria.
]

#sol-item(21, "C", dense: true)[
  Ribosomes, free in the cytoplasm or attached to the rough endoplasmic reticulum, are the site of protein synthesis.
]

#sol-item(22, "A", dense: true)[
  Bacteria have a single circular chromosome (and often plasmids) free in the cytoplasm.
]

#sol-item(23, "B", dense: true)[
  Losing the nucleus allows more haemoglobin, and therefore more oxygen, to be carried.
]

#sol-item(24, "D", dense: true)[
  Ribosomes are not enclosed in a membrane; the others are.
]

#sol-item(25, "A", dense: true)[
  The rigid cellulose wall fixes the shape; the membrane alone would give only a flexible boundary.
]

#sol-item(26, "C", dense: true)[
  Chloroplasts and the large permanent vacuole are the plant features at this level.
]

#sol-item(27, "A", dense: true)[
  The Golgi apparatus packages and secretes substances, so secretory cells are rich in it.
]

#sol-item(28, "C", dense: true)[
  Total magnification = magnification of the eyepiece lens multiplied by that of the objective lens.
]

#sol-item(29, "D", dense: true)[
  The membrane is the selectively permeable barrier of the cell.
]

#sol-item(30, "B", dense: true)[
  That is the first statement of the cell theory; the other three are false for bacteria, red blood cells and nerve cells respectively.
]

